  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "\\(\\log_2 2=1\\) and \\(\\log_2 8=3\\), so the result is \\(1/3\\).\n\nAlternative method 1: Logarithm as an exponent\n\nA logarithm asks for the exponent that produces its argument. Here \\(2^3=8\\), so \\(8^{1/3}=2\\). Hence \\(\\log_8 2=\\frac13\\).",
